content.text:
The search→geo connection is the fault. All 91 search→geo calls in the incident window took 1.4–3.0 s, while geo's own handler stayed at about 0.14 ms and the search→rate calls were unchanged. Pod network error counters stayed at zero, so this is delay in transit rather than loss.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "network_delay",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT count(*) n, round(min(duration)/1e6,1) min_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,1) p50_ms, round(max(duration)/1e6,1) max_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Client'", "claim": "All 91 search-to-geo client calls took about 1.4-3.0 s, p50 about 1.6 s."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,3) p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,3) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='geo' AND span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Server'", "claim": "Geo's own Nearby server spans stay fast, p50 about 0.14 ms, same as normal."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,2) p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,2) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND attr_span_kind='Client'", "claim": "Search's calls to rate are unchanged (p50 about 3.3 ms), so the delay is specific to the geo connection."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name pod, metric, round(avg(value),1) avg_v, round(max(value),1) max_v FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE service_name='search' AND metric IN ('k8s.pod.network.errors','k8s.pod.network.io') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Search pod network error counter stays at zero; network I/O is unchanged from normal, so this is delay, not loss."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,1) p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='search' AND span_name='search.Search/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Server') OR (service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels' AND attr_span_kind='Server') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Search's Nearby server p50 about 1.6 s matches frontend's /hotels p50 about 1.6 s; the delay passes straight up to users."}]}
  ]
}
```

